# Repo-root environment. Copy to .env (gitignored).
#
# The agent build reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; deploying reads CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN. Application
# secrets are NOT read from this file at runtime: in production they are set with
# `wrangler secret put`, and in local development they live in packages/worker/.dev.vars
# (see packages/worker/.dev.vars.example).

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# The production values, listed here so the set is documented in one place. The Worker refuses to
# serve any request in production unless all five are present, and refuses outright if
# AUTH_DISABLED is set there.
#
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID       - the OAuth 2.0 client id from Google Cloud
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET   - its client secret
#   SESSION_SECRET         - a long random string, used to sign the OAuth state value
#   PUBLIC_ORIGIN          - the app's origin, e.g. https://personal-space.workers.dev
#   ALLOWED_EMAIL          - the one Google address allowed into this space
